        {
          "id": "pub-el-b1-0033",
          "left": "274px",
          "top": "166px",
          "width": "472px",
          "height": "416px",
          "transform": "none",
          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Open Sans', 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12.5px; color:#0f172a; line-height:1.58; text-align:left; word-wrap:break-word; \"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\"><strong>Dear Shareholders and Partners,</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Fiscal year 2026 marked an inflection point for Northstar Solutions. Against tighter enterprise capital budgets across our core markets, customers prioritized measurable operational efficiency and grid resilience, expanding our total revenue from $38.9M in FY25 to $48.6M in FY26.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">Operational discipline remained central to our execution. Automated telemetry deployment lowered average onboarding duration from eleven weeks to five, lifting gross operating margin by 310 basis points while enabling 42 new engineering hires across regional support hubs.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px 0;\">In 2027, our capital roadmap focuses on regional data sovereignty, renewable microgrid orchestration, and deeper long-term customer success partnerships.</p><p style=\"margin:0; font-weight:700; color:#0f172a;\">Elena Rostova<br><span style=\"font-weight:400; color:#475569; font-size:11.5px;\">Chief Executive Officer, Northstar Solutions Ltd.</span></p></div>",
